---
/**
 * What a business can do with the guide, and what it can buy.
 *
 * Every place page ends with "Own or run X?", and this is where that leads.
 * It opens with the three things an owner can do today, free: correct a
 * listing, submit an event, send a photograph (audit priority 10, 26 October
 * 2026: lead with useful actions). Then, briefly, why the guide can be
 * trusted (a free listing is editorial and stays that way); what a listing
 * carries; the photograph rules, in the words the editorial policy uses
 * (src/lib/photo-policy.ts); what is for sale, labeled and beside the
 * editorial; and the community side, which lives on the hub's partnership
 * page. Written for the owner of a café, not for a media buyer, who has
 * /advertise/ on the hub.
 *
 * No figure, result or reader behaviour is claimed that the guide has not
 * measured: "the pages readers come back to every week" and "a listing with
 * one is read more" said what nobody had counted, and went.
 */
import Page from '@/layouts/Page.astro';
import CtaBand from '@/components/CtaBand.astro';
import TipsLink from '@/components/TipsLink.astro';
import { editionFor, emailEditions, getNetworkHub, getTown } from '@/config';
import { getTownEntries } from '@/lib/content';
import { breadcrumbJsonLd } from '@/lib/seo';
import { LAND_TYPES } from '@/content/schemas';
import { PHOTO_CREDIT, PHOTO_NOT_COPIED, PHOTO_PERMISSION, PHOTO_WANTED, photoEmailHref } from '@/lib/photo-policy';

const town = getTown();
const hub = getNetworkHub();
// The weekly email this guide is in, if any: a quiet guide or a visitor guide has none.
const edition = editionFor(town.slug, emailEditions());
const places = (await getTownEntries('places')).filter((p) => !p.delisted);
const businesses = places.filter((p) => !LAND_TYPES.includes(p.data.type)).length;
// The directory counts every place, parks and trails included; this page is
// for the businesses among them, and says both so the two pages agree.
const land = places.length - businesses;
// With no form configured the contact page falls back to a mailto link, so
// the claim link and the sentence about it say that instead of promising a
// pre-filled form that is not there.
const hasForm = Boolean(town.formspreeId);
const claim = hasForm ? `/contact/?about=${encodeURIComponent('My business')}#message-form` : '/contact/';
const partner = `mailto:${hub.social.email}?subject=${encodeURIComponent(`Partnership — ${town.siteTitle}`)}`;
// A photograph cannot go through the forms (Formspree takes no files here),
// so it is an email, with the permission questions already in it.
const photo = photoEmailHref(hub.social.email, town.siteTitle);
const advertise = `https://${hub.domain}/advertise/`;
// /advertise/ shows a rate card only once `hub.rates` is set; until then it
// makes the founding offer without a price.
const hasRates = (hub.rates?.length ?? 0) > 0;
const description = `If you run a business in ${town.name}, ${town.state}: correct your free listing, submit an event, or send a photograph. Listings are editorial; sponsorship is labeled and sits beside them.`;
// The three actions, in the order an owner most often needs them.
const actions = [
  {
    title: 'Correct a listing',
    body: 'Wrong hours, a new phone number, a move, a closing or a new name. Say what has changed; we check it against your own website or another source and fix it, usually within a day or two.',
    label: 'Report a correction',
    href: '/correct/',
  },
  {
    title: 'Submit an event',
    body: 'Anything open to the public, such as a tasting, a class or a market day, goes on the events calendar for nothing. We need the date, the time and a link to your own page about it.',
    label: 'Submit an event',
    href: '/submit-event/',
  },
  {
    title: 'Send a photograph',
    body: 'One you took or hold the rights to, with how to credit it. The email opens with the questions we need answered.',
    label: 'Email a photograph',
    href: photo,
    more: '#photographs',
  },
];
---
<Page
  title="For businesses"
  seoTitle={`For businesses in ${town.name}: fix a listing, add an event, send a photo`}
  eyebrow={town.siteTitle}
  {description}
  intro={`If you run something in ${town.name}, here are three things you can do today, all free. Below them: how the guide stays independent, what a listing carries, and what is for sale.`}
  jsonLd={breadcrumbJsonLd(town, [
    { name: town.name, path: '/' },
    { name: 'For businesses', path: '/for-businesses/' },
  ])}
  narrow
>
  <ul class="grid gap-4" role="list" aria-label="Things you can do now">
    {actions.map((a) => (
      <li class="rounded-lg bg-raised p-5 ring-1 ring-line-soft sm:flex sm:items-center sm:justify-between sm:gap-6 md:p-6">
        <div>
          <h2 class="text-[1.25rem] font-semibold leading-snug">{a.title}</h2>
          <p class="mt-1.5 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
            {a.body}
            {a.more && <Fragment>{' '}<a href={a.more} class="text-primary underline">The photograph rules</a>.</Fragment>}
          </p>
        </div>
        <a href={a.href} class="btn btn-primary mt-4 w-full shrink-0 justify-center sm:mt-0 sm:w-auto">{a.label}</a>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>

  <div class="prose mt-14">
    <h2>How the guide stays independent</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Listings are free and editorial. Nobody can pay to be listed, to be placed higher, to be called a pick, or to have a listing taken down.</li>
      <li>Every listing is checked against a source, usually your own website, and shows the day it was last checked.</li>
      <li>We write the listing from the facts; we do not publish wording a business dictates, or remove a listing because a competitor asked.</li>
      <li>Sponsorship, where it is sold, is labeled as sponsorship and sits beside the listings, never inside them. It buys nothing in them.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The <a href="/editorial/">editorial policy</a> has the detail, and it binds us as much as anyone.</p>

    <h2>What a listing carries</h2>
    <p>
      {town.siteTitle} lists {businesses} businesses and venues in {town.name}{land > 0 && <Fragment>, and {land} parks and trails beside them, {places.length} places in all</Fragment>}, because they are here, not because
      anyone paid. A listing carries your name, what you are, where you are, when you are open, your phone number
      and your website, a sentence or two on what you are known for, and a photograph if we have one we are allowed
      to use. It shows whether you are open right now, worked out from the hours on the page, and it appears in the
      <a href="/directory/">directory</a>, in the <a href="/search/">site search</a>, and beside any event held at
      your address.
    </p>
    <p>
      Every place page has an “Own or run this?” link at the foot of its details, which reports a correction about
      that listing. For hours, one line in your words is best, such as “Tue–Sat 10–5; closed Sun–Mon”: we keep it in
      that shape so the site can tell readers when you are open. <TipsLink class="" />.
    </p>
    <p>
      Not listed at all? <a href={claim}>Tell us</a>{hasForm ? ' on the contact form' : ' by email'}. If you are in
      {' '}{town.name} and open to the public, you belong here.
    </p>

    <h2 id="photographs">Photographs</h2>
    <p>
      Most listings have no photograph, and one from you is welcome. {PHOTO_WANTED}
    </p>
    <p>{PHOTO_PERMISSION} {PHOTO_NOT_COPIED}</p>
    <p>
      {PHOTO_CREDIT} <a href="/credits/">See the photo credits</a>. To send one, <a href={photo}>email it to
      {' '}{hub.social.email}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>What is for sale</h2>
    <p>
      Sponsorship, labeled as such, beside the editorial and never inside it. A sponsor’s name appears on a
      page{hub.newsletter && edition && ' or in the weekly email'} as “presented by”, with a link. It does not change a listing, the order of a
      list, or what we write. The placements on this guide are:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>A “presented by” line on the <a href="/events/">events page</a> and the <a href="/this-weekend/">weekend page</a>, which list what is on each week.</li>
      <li>A labeled block on <a href="/moving-here/">Moving here</a>, the guide’s page for people about to move to {town.name}.</li>
      {hub.newsletter && edition && (
        <li>
          {edition.shared
            ? `A line at the top of the weekly email for ${edition.name}, which ${town.name} shares with its neighbors; one sponsor reaches all of it.`
            : `A line at the top of the weekly ${town.siteTitle} email.`}
        </li>
      )}
    </ul>
    {/* This said prices and audience figures were on /advertise/, which
        publishes neither until there are numbers to stand behind (audit, 7
        October 2026). It now says what that page holds in whichever state it
        is in. The second line is the network sponsor, which /this-weekend/
        and the Nearby block carry beside a town's own. */}
    <p>
      One sponsor per placement, so a sponsor is not competing with three others on the same page: the most a page
      carries is that one and the network’s own sponsor line, which is sold for every guide at once and labeled the
      same way.
      {hasRates ? (
        <Fragment>
          Prices are on the network’s <a href={advertise}>advertising page</a>, with what the guides have measured of
          their audience and since when.
        </Fragment>
      ) : (
        <Fragment>
          Prices are not published yet: ask, and we will quote one. The network’s <a href={advertise}>advertising
          page</a> says what has been measured so far and since when, and quotes no number nobody counted.
        </Fragment>
      )}
      To talk about a placement, <a href={partner}>email us</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Chambers and community groups</h2>
    <p>
      A chamber, a library, a recreation district or a volunteer group can work with the guide for nothing: sharing
      verified events, sending corrections and closures, and planning seasonal guides. The network’s
      <a href={`${advertise}#community`}>partnership page</a> says how, with a labeled example of what a small first
      pilot could look like. It is an example only: no partnership is implied by it, and none buys a place in the
      listings.
    </p>
  </div>
  {/* The page's actions again, at its foot. */}
  <CtaBand
    slot="after"
    eyebrow="For businesses"
    title="Something to add or fix?"
    links={[
      { label: 'Correct a listing', href: '/correct/', primary: true },
      { label: 'Submit an event', href: '/submit-event/' },
      { label: 'Send a photograph', href: photo },
    ]}
  />
</Page>
